CHAPTER I
GENERAL PROVISIONS
Article 1
In this Regional Regulation, what is meant by:
1. Regional Government is the Government of Sumenep Regency;
2. Regent is the Regent of Sumenep;
3. Regional Apparatus is an organization/institution within the Regional Government that is responsible to the Regional Head in the context of administering government consisting of the Regional Secretariat, Regional Agencies and Regional Technical Institutions, Sub-districts and Civil Service Police Units according to regional needs;
4. Implementation is a form of executing protection for women and children victims of violence;
5. Child is a person who has not yet reached 18 years of age, including those in the womb;
6. Violence is any unlawful act that results in or may result in misery or suffering whether physical, sexual, economic, social, psychological to the victim;
7. Violence against Women is any action that results in or may result in misery or suffering of women physically, sexually, economically, socially, psychologically, including threats of certain actions, coercion or deprivation of freedom, whether occurring in public or private life;
8. Violence against children is any action that results in or may result in discrimination, exploitation, whether economic or sexual, neglect, cruelty, abuse, injustice and other mistreatment;
9. Physical Violence is any act that causes pain, injury, wounds or disability to a person's body, miscarriage, fainting and/or causes death;
10. Sexual Violence is any act in the form of sexual harassment, forced sexual intercourse, forced sexual intercourse in an unnatural or unwanted manner, forced sexual intercourse with others for commercial purposes and/or certain purposes;
11. Economic violence is any act that neglects family members in the form of not providing livelihood, care or maintenance as appropriate;
12. Psychological Violence is any act that results in fear, loss of self-confidence, loss of ability to act, feelings of helplessness and/or severe psychological suffering in a person;
13. Victim is women and children who experience misery and/or suffering either directly or indirectly as a result of violence;
14. Protection of Women is all activities aimed at providing a sense of security carried out by the police, prosecutor's office, courts, social institutions, or other parties who know or hear that violence against women will occur or has occurred;
15. Child Protection is all activities to guarantee and protect children and their rights so they can live, grow, develop and participate optimally in accordance with human dignity and receive protection from violence and discrimination;
16. Integrated Service Center for the Protection of Women and Children hereinafter abbreviated as P2TP2A is a service center that has the duties and functions of coordinating with related agencies in the formulation of technical policies and implementation in the field of prevention and eradication as well as elimination of acts of violence against children and women, implementation of prevention and eradication of acts of violence against women and children in accordance with the provisions of applicable Laws and Regulations as well as implementation of policies and prevention of problems in the field;
17. Community Social Institution is a Non-Governmental Organization (NGO) and/or other community organizations;
18. Population is Indonesian citizens and foreigners who enter legally and reside in the territory of Indonesia.

REGENT OF SUMENEP
a. that the number of acts of violence against women and children in Sumenep Regency is still high, while services and protection for women and children in Sumenep Regency have not been carried out optimally;
b. that in the framework of implementing regional autonomy, the regulation and service to the community, especially for women and children victims of violence, is the duty and function of the regency government because violence against women and children is a violation of Human Rights; that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence in the Regional Regulation of Sumenep Regency.
